  "imagery": "King County GIS, KingCo_Aerial_2019",
  "imagery_note": "LEAF-ON at 28.3% vegetation cover (Denver's leaf-off reference is 7.2%), and 0.101 m/px -- a ramp is ~15 px against Denver's ~26. The least leafy King County year, which is the best available: Seattle's own sharper caches are EPSG:2926 and the tile math does not apply. Adequate to size a LARGE error, which is what a Poor-anchor calibration needs; NOT adequate to grade a city expected to be Good, and the unjudgeable rate will be high with a selection effect toward un-treed corners.",
